# Foundations: media queries, keyboard-aware app height, safe areas, touch targets

## What to build

The shared groundwork that makes graph-manager's web UI (`apps/graph-manager/src/web`) usable on a phone. Later tasks (the phone nav, the page layouts, the terminal keyboard work) build on it, so the names below are a contract and must be exact.

1. A new module `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/media.ts` with the app's media queries (`NARROW`, `PHONE`, `COARSE`) and a `useMedia(query)` hook. `pages/Terminals.tsx` drops its private `useNarrow()` and uses `useMedia(NARROW)`.
2. A new module `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/viewport.ts` with a `useVisualViewport()` hook, called once in `Shell.tsx`. It keeps a CSS variable `--app-h` on `<html>` equal to the visual viewport height (the space above the phone keyboard), toggles the class `kb-open` on `<html>` while the on-screen keyboard is open, and stops iOS from scrolling the page up under the top. It also exports the pure function `isKeyboardOpen()`.
3. `index.html` gets a phone-ready viewport meta and `theme-color` metas.
4. `Shell.css` sizes the app with `var(--app-h, 100dvh)` instead of `100dvh` and pads the iPhone notch / home bar with `env(safe-area-inset-*)`. Toasts, drawer footers and dialogs clear the home bar too.
5. `ui/base.css` gets one `@media (pointer: coarse)` block: every button, icon button, tab, chip-button, list row and nav control has a hit area of at least 40 × 40 px, and every text input/select/textarea uses `font-size: 16px` so iOS Safari doesn't zoom in on focus. Desktop (fine pointer) sizes do not change at all.

Out of scope here (other tasks do them, do NOT add them): the phone top bar / nav drawer, PWA tags (`<link rel="manifest">`, `apple-touch-icon`, `apple-mobile-web-app-*`, `mobile-web-app-capable`), page layouts (cards below 600 px), the terminal extra-keys row and terminal touch handling, `Terminals.css` changes.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx` (lines 44–59 and line 92) — the private `NARROW` constant and `useNarrow()` hook to replace; line 92 is its only call (`const narrow = useNarrow();`). `narrow` is then used at :155, :332, :449–494, :537, :576 — leave those uses alone.
