  - `.drawer` (:185–189): add `padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top);` (the panel is `position: fixed; top: 0`, its header would sit under the notch).
  - `.drawer-footer` (:193): `padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6) calc(var(--space-4) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));`. Add `.drawer-body:last-child { padding-bottom: calc(var(--space-5) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }` for drawers without a footer.
  - `.dialog-overlay` (:200–203): each side of the padding becomes `calc(var(--space-4) + env(safe-area-inset-<side>))`.
- **IMPLEMENT** (touch block, append at the very end of the file):
  ```css
  /* Touch screens: every control gets a 40 x 40 px hit area (icons keep their size); 16 px inputs so iOS doesn't zoom. */
  @media (pointer: coarse) {
    .btn, .btn-sm, .dialog-actions .btn, .empty-state .btn { min-height: 40px; }
    .btn-icon, .btn-icon.btn-sm { min-width: 40px; }
    html .segmented { height: 40px; }
    .segmented-option { min-width: 40px; }
    button.chip, a.chip, button.run-chip { min-height: 40px; }
    .table-row[tabindex], a.table-row, .table-row.clickable { min-height: 40px; }
    .toast-action { min-width: 40px; min-height: 40px; }
    /* Nav and palette (Shell.css) */
    .nav-item, .status-row, .nav-jump, .palette-item { min-height: 40px; }
    .nav-icon-btn, .nav-logout { min-width: 40px; min-height: 40px; }
    /* Terminals (pages/Terminals.css) */
    .terms-tab { min-height: 40px; }
    .terms-tab-close, .tp-icon, .tp-foot-chip, .terms-layouts button { min-width: 40px; min-height: 40px; }
    html .tp-head, html .tp-foot { height: auto; min-height: 40px; }
    input:not([type="checkbox"]):not([type="radio"]):not([type="range"]):not([type="button"]):not([type="submit"]), select, textarea { font-size: 16px !important; }
  }
  ```
- **GOTCHA**:
  - Use `min-width` / `min-height`, never `width` / `height`, for the hit areas: `min-*` beats `width`/`height` whatever their specificity or file order, so the page CSS (`.tp-icon { width: 22px }`, `.terms-tab-close { width: 18px }`) need not change, and the icons inside (`<Icon size=…>`) stay the same size.
  - `.segmented-option` already has `min-width: 0` in base.css (:172); the coarse block comes later in the same file, so it wins.
  - `.tp-head` (32 px) and `.tp-foot` (30 px) have a fixed `height` in Terminals.css; with 40 px children they must grow, hence `height: auto` with the `html` prefix (one extra element in specificity so it beats Terminals.css regardless of bundle order).
  - The font-size needs `!important`: many inputs set a class-level `font` shorthand (`.input` 13px at :64, `.palette-input` 14px in Shell.css:122, `.terms-tab-input` 12px in Terminals.css:85) that an element selector would otherwise lose to.
  - `.tsb-item` (Terminals sidebar row) is already `min-height: 52px`; leave it. `.chip` spans used as labels (`<span className="chip">` in Projects/Workspaces) must not grow, which is why only `button.chip, a.chip` are listed.
  - Do NOT put these rules in `pages/Terminals.css` (another task edits that file; keeping them in base.css avoids merge conflicts).
  - No control in the app is visible only on `:hover` today (checked); keep it that way.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run lint`

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/media.test.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT** (jsdom, `renderHook` + `act`):
  ```typescript
  // @vitest-environment jsdom
  import { act, renderHook } from "@testing-library/react";
  import { afterEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from "vitest";
  import { COARSE, NARROW, PHONE, useMedia } from "./media";

  /** A fake MediaQueryList whose `matches` can be flipped with `set()`; fires `change` like a browser. */
  function stubMedia(initial: Record<string, boolean>) {
    const state = { ...initial };
    const listeners = new Map<string, Set<() => void>>();
    vi.stubGlobal("matchMedia", vi.fn((q: string) => ({
      get matches() { return state[q] ?? false; },
      media: q,
      addEventListener: (_: string, fn: () => void) => { (listeners.get(q) ?? listeners.set(q, new Set()).get(q)!).add(fn); },
      removeEventListener: (_: string, fn: () => void) => { listeners.get(q)?.delete(fn); },
    })));
    return { set(q: string, v: boolean) { state[q] = v; listeners.get(q)?.forEach((fn) => fn()); }, listeners };
  }
  afterEach(() => vi.unstubAllGlobals());
  ```
  Cases: the constants equal `"(max-width: 899.98px)"`, `"(max-width: 599.98px)"`, `"(pointer: coarse)"`; with no `matchMedia` (jsdom default; `vi.stubGlobal("matchMedia", undefined)` to be sure) `useMedia(NARROW)` is `false`; stubbed `true` → `true`; stubbed `false` → `false`; after `act(() => m.set(NARROW, true))` the result turns `true` and back on `false`; after `unmount()` the listener set for that query is empty.
