## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `ui/media.ts` exports `NARROW = "(max-width: 899.98px)"`, `PHONE = "(max-width: 599.98px)"`, `COARSE = "(pointer: coarse)"` and `useMedia(query): boolean`, which follows `change` events and returns `false` without `window.matchMedia`.
- [ ] `pages/Terminals.tsx` has no `useNarrow` and no local `NARROW`; it uses `useMedia(NARROW)` and behaves as before (`Terminals.test.tsx` passes unchanged).
- [ ] `ui/viewport.ts` exports `useVisualViewport()`, `isKeyboardOpen(vvHeight, innerHeight, activeIsEditable)` and `isEditable(el)`. `Shell` calls `useVisualViewport()` once.
- [ ] With a visual viewport of height H, `<html>` has `style="--app-h: Hpx"`; with an editable element focused and H < innerHeight − 120, `<html>` has class `kb-open`; it is removed when focus leaves or the viewport grows back; both are removed on unmount. `offsetTop > 0` → `window.scrollTo(0, 0)`.
- [ ] `index.html` viewport meta is exactly `width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover, interactive-widget=resizes-content`, plus two `theme-color` metas (`#ffffff` light, `#16181b` dark). No manifest / apple-* tags.
- [ ] `Shell.css` has no `100dvh` left except as the `var(--app-h, 100dvh)` fallback; `.gm-shell` pads `env(safe-area-inset-top/right/left)`; toasts, drawer header/footer and dialog overlay clear the safe areas.
- [ ] On a `pointer: coarse` device every `.btn`, icon button, tab, tab close, pane-header icon, footer chip, nav item, palette item, segmented option, clickable table row and toast action has a hit box ≥ 40 × 40 px, and `input`/`select`/`textarea` compute to 16 px. On a desktop (fine pointer) nothing changes size.
- [ ] Tests pass: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/ui/media.test.ts src/web/ui/viewport.test.ts src/web/Shell.test.tsx src/web/pages/Terminals.test.tsx`

